# Template: Basic Requirements Structure

## File Purpose
This template provides a basic structure for Tyler to write requirements for simple enhancements. It focuses solely on giving structure to the initial requirements.md file.

## Usage
```
create-template: rules-workflow @template-basic.mdc
```

## Requirements Template

When this template is applied, it will create the following structure in requirements.md:

```markdown
# [Feature Name] Requirements

## Objective
[What is the goal of this enhancement?]

## Success Criteria
[What measurable outcomes will indicate success?]

## Technical Requirements
[What specific technical changes are needed?]

## Constraints
[What limitations or requirements must be considered?]
```

## Template Application

When the create-template command is received, I will:
1. Create or update requirements.md with this template
2. Leave all sections empty for Tyler to fill in
3. Wait for Tyler to complete the requirements before proceeding with any planning

## Next Steps
1. Tyler fills in the requirements template with enhancement details
2. Once requirements are complete, Tyler initiates planning with:
   ```
   plan-mode: rules-workflow @template-basic.mdc
   ```

## Use Cases
- Simple syntax updates
- Documentation improvements
- Minor feature additions
- Straightforward bug fixes 